; The dev overlay: what a tool outside the game shows about it and edits in it.
;
; Above camlcast rather than beside it. core, loom and lib are three libraries
; with a rule about which may know what; this is a fourth that knows all of
; them and that none of them knows. Nothing in those three names this one, and
; a game that ships does not link it -- which is the whole reason it is a
; library of its own rather than a corner of lib/.
;
; It names camlcast.loom directly and not only through camlcast, because what
; it reads -- Trace events, Path, the slot view -- is loom's own vocabulary and
; camlcast re-exports only part of it. (implicit_transitive_deps false) makes
; that an explicit line rather than something inherited.
;
; compiler-libs.common is the compiler's own parser, and it is here to find
; where expressions are and for nothing else. Span parses to locate and then
; splices bytes; it never prints OCaml, so the part of that library this
; depends on is the part that does not move between releases.
;
; -w +70 for the reason the other three carry it: every module here has an
; .mli, and the flag is what keeps the next one from arriving without one.

(library
 (flags
  (:standard -w +70))
 (name camlcast_edit)
 (public_name camlcast.edit)
 (libraries camlcast camlcast_core camlcast_loom compiler-libs.common))
